# The archive is append only, so two runs that both appended to the same month
# file have not really conflicted: both sets of lines are wanted. Git's built in
# union driver keeps both sides instead of stopping a rebase for a conflict that
# has an obvious correct resolution.
#
# Order after a union merge is not guaranteed, so nothing that reads the archive
# may depend on file order alone. Readers sort by the timestamp on the record,
# and the loader deduplicates, so a line appearing twice is harmless.
data/archive/*.ndjson merge=union

# Keep the archive and the fixture byte for byte across platforms. A rewritten
# line ending would change every digest in the file.
*.ndjson -text
fixtures/* -text
